From 7f63af2af15152ff015c1015c27d1dd2a644df12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:50:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the tab bar always visible so its transition animation
 shows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hiding the bar whenever an overlay opened meant it vanished before
you could ever see the pill slide to the new tab. Reverts that in
both AdminPanel.js and ClientView.js — the bar now stays floating on
top at all times. This is safe because every full-screen sub-view
already reserves paddingBottom:80 for its scrollable content (more
than the bar's ~65px footprint), and the exercise-picker/edit modals
sit at a higher z-index (1100/1150) than the bar so they still cover
it correctly while genuinely open. Also gave ProgressPhotos.js the
same paddingBottom:80 the other sub-screens already had — it was
missing it, so its bottom content would've been covered now that the
bar never hides.
---
 src/AdminPanel.js     | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 src/ClientView.js     |  6 +--
 src/ProgressPhotos.js |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/AdminPanel.js b/src/AdminPanel.js
index b3bd050..49e8d0a 100644
--- a/src/AdminPanel.js
+++ b/src/AdminPanel.js
@@ -814,52 +814,52 @@ export default function AdminPanel({ user, onLogout }) {
       </div>
 
